{"name":"Potted Plant","hex":"#9ecca7","fetched":"2026-10-12","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"potted plant","whole":true,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A plant which has been planted in a container, often a houseplant.","A shill taking part in an auction."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/potted_plant"}],"entries":[{"title":"Houseplant","blocks":[{"text":"A houseplant, also known as a pot plant, potted plant, or indoor plant, is an ornamental plant cultivated indoors for aesthetic or practical purposes. These plants are commonly found in homes, offices, and various indoor spaces, where they contribute to the ambiance by adding natural beauty and improving air quality. Most houseplants are tropical or semi-tropical species, as they thrive in the warm, humid conditions often found indoors. Many of them are epiphytes, succulents, or cacti, which are particularly well-suited to indoor environments due to their low maintenance requirements."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/6/6d/Orkide_i_finstua_mot_vest.jpg/330px-Orkide_i_finstua_mot_vest.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Houseplant"},{"title":"Container garden","blocks":[{"text":"Container gardening or pot gardening/farming is the practice of growing plants, including edible plants, exclusively in containers instead of planting them in the ground. A container in gardening is a small, enclosed and usually portable object used for displaying live flowers or plants. It may take the form of a pot, box, tub, basket, tin, barrel or hanging basket."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/9/94/Container_garden_on_front_porch.jpg/330px-Container_garden_on_front_porch.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Container_garden"},{"title":"Plant","blocks":[{"text":"Plants are the eukaryotic organisms that constitute the kingdom Plantae. They are predominantly photosynthetic or came from photosynthetic ancestors, meaning that they obtain their energy from sunlight by using the green pigment chlorophyll in their chloroplasts to produce sugars from carbon dioxide and water. Over the course of time, some plants have evolved to be parasitic, meaning they take energy from other organisms. Except for glaucophytes, some green algae and a few red algae, most plants are multicellular."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/5/57/Fr%C3%BChling_bl%C3%BChender_Kirschenbaum.jpg/330px-Fr%C3%BChling_bl%C3%BChender_Kirschenbaum.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Plant"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/8/8c/Blomsterf%C3%B6nstret_av_Carl_Larsson_1894.jpg/500px-Blomsterf%C3%B6nstret_av_Carl_Larsson_1894.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/8/8c/Blomsterf%C3%B6nstret_av_Carl_Larsson_1894.jpg/1280px-Blomsterf%C3%B6nstret_av_Carl_Larsson_1894.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/8/8c/Blomsterf%C3%B6nstret_av_Carl_Larsson_1894.jpg/500px-Blomsterf%C3%B6nstret_av_Carl_Larsson_1894.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"\"Flowers on the Windowsill\", 1894","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3ABlomsterf%C3%B6nstret_av_Carl_Larsson_1894.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/9/9a/Francisco_de_Zurbar%C3%A1n_-_Still_Life_with_Lemons%2C_Oranges_and_a_Rose%2C1633.png/500px-Francisco_de_Zurbar%C3%A1n_-_Still_Life_with_Lemons%2C_Oranges_and_a_Rose%2C1633.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/9/9a/Francisco_d